cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If this specification informs your work, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "Traffic Agentic Engineering: An Open Specification of Traffic Agent Cognition"
type: dataset
abstract: >-
  Traffic Agentic Engineering (TAE) is an open specification describing how AI agents
  should carry engineering responsibility in transportation domains. It defines a
  compilation-oriented architecture -- Responsibility, Engineering IR, Reasoning Planner,
  Engineering Primitive, Primitive Dependency Graph, Compiler, Validation, Delivery --
  and a semantic contract (Traffic Primitive Specification, TPS) under which engineering
  primitives such as traffic.queue.length are named by engineering meaning rather than
  by implementation, enabling reproducible and auditable reasoning across swappable
  computational operators. Volume I (Chapters 1--9) complete; v0.1 draft.
